{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108032","id":2622731551,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6cU7Uf","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108032","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108032.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108032.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108032","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108032/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/108032/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108032/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/eb7fda0ccb5b668a1d7a0a5843b030cabd097292","number":108032,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Jolt Physics: Fix crash if a soft body is disabled","user":{"login":"simpkins","id":163549,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzU0OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/163549?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins","html_url":"https://github.com/simpkins","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"If a `SoftBody3D` object is disabled, its default behavior is to remove itself from the physics server by calling\r\n`PhysicsServer3D::soft_body_set_mesh()` to reset the mesh to an empty RID.\r\n\r\nWith the Jolt physics server, this causes a crash.\r\n\r\nThe `JoltSoftBody3D` code generally assumes that the `jolt_settings` member variable is null when the body is actively part of a space (when `in_space()` returns true), and non-null when the body is not part of a space.  However, calling `JoltSoftBody3D::set_mesh()` with a null RID moves the body out of the space, but does not re-allocate the `jolt_settings` member variable.  This causes a crash when the code tries to access it later in the `set_mesh()` call (inside `_space_changed()`, which tries to update pressure in the `jolt_settings` object).\r\n\r\nThis fixes that problem by ensuring that the `jolt_settings` object is always re-allocated whenever we clear the `shared` member variable.\r\n\r\nFixes #108030.\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch in priority.\r\n\r\nRelevant fixes are cherry-picked for stable branches as needed by maintainers.\r\n\r\nTo speed up the contribution process and avoid CI errors, please set up pre-commit hooks locally:\r\nhttps://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/contributing/development/code_style_guidelines.html\r\n-->\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":370471880,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzA0NzE4ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:physics","name":"topic:physics","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1327318271,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMzI3M